"@type": "Question",
"name": "What is the best JLPT online course?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "It depends on what you need. Coto Academy is the strongest all-around pick if you want live instruction, professional JLPT instructors, and flexible scheduling. J-Standard is best if you want a self-paced, affordable option without live classes. Preply suits learners who want 1-on-1 tutoring and are willing to vet tutors themselves. There's no single \"best\" course for everyone — the right one depends on your level, budget, time zone, and whether you want live or self-paced instruction.

"
}
}
, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "Are JLPT online courses actually effective?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Yes, as long as the course is built around the exam rather than general conversation. A good JLPT course gives you timed mock tests, exam-specific strategy, and focused practice on the sections the real test weights heavily, like grammar and reading — things self-study and conversation-based classes typically don't cover in depth.

"
}
}
, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "How long does it take to prepare for the JLPT with an online course?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "It varies by level and course. Short intensives like Kudan Institute or SNG run 2–3 months and are designed as a final push before the exam. Longer programs like Coto Academy's one-year track suit learners building proficiency from the ground up. As a rule, the higher the level (N2, N1), the more prep time you should budget.

"
}
}
, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "How much do JLPT online courses cost?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Pricing ranges widely: J-Standard starts around $69 for 3 months, Japonin runs from about ¥1,280 per lesson, and structured short-term intensives like SNG or Kudan run roughly ¥39,600–¥49,500 for a 2–3 month course. Live 1-on-1 tutoring through Preply is the most expensive per hour ($20–$70), since you're paying for individual attention.

"
}
}
, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "Do I need to already know Japanese to join a JLPT online course?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Most courses assume some prior study. J-Standard is the exception, starting from hiragana and katakana for true beginners. Others, like SNG, require a minimum number of self-study hours (300+ for N3, 600+ for N2) before enrolling.
